## How it was tested

- `content:skills:fishing`: new `FishBarrelMessagesTest` (5 unit tests: the empty text, one fish type, several types separated by commas, the split into a second box after eight types, the full and empty-barrel destroy texts). `spotlessCheck` passes.
- In game, desktop RuneLite against this branch:
  - Check on an empty barrel opened the item box with the barrel and "The barrel is empty.", and no game messages.
  - After Fill with 3 raw shrimps and 2 raw anchovies, Check showed "The barrel contains:<br>2 x Raw anchovies, 3 x Raw shrimps".
  - Fill on a full barrel (28 fish) sent "The barrel is full. It may be emptied at a bank."
  - Destroy on the full barrel showed the confirmation with the filled note. No kept the barrel and its 28 fish; Yes removed it.
  - A new open barrel then showed the empty note on Destroy, and Yes removed it.

## Checklist

- [x] Builds and the server boots
- [x] Tests only cover complex logic and anything that moves items (no dupes): the Check texts; Destroy only deletes the clicked slot after the confirmation
- [x] Gamevals symbols instead of raw ids; game data in the cache, not Kotlin maps: destroy notes come from the item params; the empty-barrel note isn't in the cache, so it is a constant
- [ ] State in varbits/varps, not attrs: the barrel's contents stay in #191's attr; not changed here
- [x] Matches the OSRS wiki (deviations noted in `docs/quirks.md`): see the notes below
- [ ] New content checked against rsprox dumps where possible: rsprox.net has no recording with a fish barrel (searched by its obj ids and texts)
- [x] No unrelated or hand-edited generated changes (spotless also moved one import in the file)

## Screenshots / notes for reviewers

Sources: the wiki's [Fish barrel](https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fish_barrel) page (Check, the full message, the infobox's Destroy notes for an empty and a filled barrel), the cache (ops `Fill, Check, Open/Close, -, Destroy`; `destroy_note_desc`), and the texts that RuneLite plugins expect (the Fish Barrel hub plugin's parser and its test: `The barrel contains:<br>1 x Raw anglerfish, 2 x Raw monkfish, ...`).

Not confirmed by any source:
- How the official server splits a very long list. Here more than eight fish types continue in a second box, without the header.
- Which action sends the full message. Here it's Fill on a full barrel. Catching fish into a full open barrel stays silent, as before.
- Whether destroying one of two barrels loses the shared contents. Here the contents are kept until the last barrel goes.

